{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/765215-how-common-should-changing-breeds-be","id":765215,"title":"How common should changing breeds be?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-13T16:41:52-08:00","id":765215,"title":"How common should changing breeds be?","content":"So the chronicle is set in and around a fictional coastal American city of about seven million (I've not yet figured out a name. I think It'll be the west coast). Unfortunately I don't have the book on changing breeds. I've only read the corebook, book of the wyrm and the all-important cookbook. (I've read a LOT on other world of darkness games though)<br /> <br /> I'm considering adding<br /> - one other group of garou. Maybe two. Possibly three. What should I even mean when I say group? Like septs or packs or..What's appropriate for a city of six million?<br /> -sharks<br /> -Apes<br /> -A bastet.<br /> -A Rhino. For kicks.<br /> -Something else rare, not in the books, bizzare and undeniably wyrm. (but it fits)<br /> -a spider<br /> - Ratkin for the end. (or sharks, Or cthulu)<br /> <br /> But now I realise that, well, my game might as well be a <b>trip to the zoo</b>. Yeah, they're not going to be introduced all at once, and I can put a story or two around each of them (especially the Rokea, but the rhino really is there primarily for a bizarre surprise) Mix them in with fomori, ghouls, Leeches, spirits, that one cult, and maybe a mage if enough things go wrong, and you've essentially got a very colourful world of darkness. These things are supposed to be rare, but how rare?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T17:15:13-08:00","id":765238,"title":"","content":"Only add what you feel is necessary for the story you want to tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T18:29:16-08:00","id":765269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/765215-how-common-should-changing-breeds-be?p=765238#post765238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only add what you feel is necessary for the story you want to tell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Completely agree.<br /> <br /> Once you figure out what story you want to run, you can figure out how much you need to do.<br /> <br /> Here are some guidelines.<br /> <br /> Garou don't work well by solely using population to determine their numbers. A large metropolis may hardly have any Garou because there are no caerns there, and there aren't enough kinfolk to maintain a population. Some rural area in Montana that is sparsely populated may have dozens of Garou because of the local wildlife and that there are several small settlements in the region with lots of kinfolk. So you can go from Garou being 1 for every million, to 1 Garou for every thousand or ten thousand people in the region.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, Garou chronicles likely cover a much larger geographic area than something like vampire which is really based on a single vampire population center (the city). Garou chronicles typically need multiple septs, with each sept having a caern of different ranks and probably a different tribal structure for each one. The game might be based out of one sept to serve as a base for the PCs, but the PCs will likely need to visit many septs over the course of the chronicle as they rise in rank, need to consult specific Garou, or just look for different quests.<br /> <br /> Sept population is usually determined by the importance of the caern. Higher ranked caerns have higher population of Garou to protect them. Generally it's around 5-10 Garou per rank of the Caern.<br /> <br /> Assuming you will want players to go from Rank 1 to 5, you will need caerns of each rank (as to learn Gifts they need to be at a caern at the level of the Gift). Personally, I would not have only five caerns (one for each level). I would keep any caerns at the local level at low levels (1-3) and make rank 4 or 5 caerns &quot;out of region&quot; in order to demonstrate their rarity. Those large caerns may or may not have moonbridges to one of the local caerns the players will know, but probably at least one.<br /> <br /> So you have your city in southern California. It may have one or more urban caerns controlled by Bone Gnawers or Glasswalkers, but open to other tribes. Importance will depend on what the city is known for. If it is an important center of finance, entertainment, industry, high technology, etc. it may have an important caern based on that. If not, probably a low rank. Then you'll want several caerns of different levels in the local region. That region may not only be southern California, but also parts of Arizona, Nevada, and northern Mexico. Then based on the Tribe and Auspice of your PCs, you may want to give some though to more powerful caerns farther away they can travel to at the right time - something in the Midwest, Canada, or even overseas.<br /> <br /> If you don't want to get big, you can keep a few septs that are very small in numbers. You'll know best how big in scope you need for the game. You can always start small and then make it larger as you need it.<br /> <br /> Only bring in other Changing Breeds if they are absolutely essential to the story you want to tell. Usually you can accomplish what you need with another Garou. If you do have one, make sure the species its from is native to the region. Southern california has some options, but a weretiger or werelion probably doesn't make sense while a were-cougar would.<br /> <br /> As for Fomori or other Wyrm creatures, figure out what the local bad guys are, and you'll know what to include.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T21:09:32-08:00","id":765329,"title":"","content":"If you want a Zoo make a zoo. w20 is all about play/run what you want. Presumably your fictional city was basically put on the map by the Gold Rush. Lot of Asians came over then, enough of them were Kin that you had the Hengeyokai take notice. A sentai finds the caern abandoned and took up guarding it, rather than let it fall the wyrm they decided to abit of prostilyzing among their western kin so you have a modern setup that has multibreed &quot;Packs&quot; and multiple breeds sharing the same sept. They might have some Asian hold overs or not(If some of the founders were Kitsune they might even still be around!)<br /> <br /> This will let you have all sorts of fun nonwyrmy conflict as various groups attack the sept for its Impurity(garou, various breeds etc) along with your standard wyrmy bits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T23:51:21-08:00","id":765402,"title":"","content":"I would disagree with &quot;only bring in other changing breeds if they are absolutely essential to the story you want to tell.&quot;<br /> <br /> I would say &quot;bring in other changing breeds if you want.&quot; Bringing in other changing breeds necessarily brings other stuff up - conflicts, for example - that are worth exploring. Garou should make up the majority, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T02:11:27-08:00","id":769050,"title":"","content":"The story is key. Many years ago now, before Revised I ran a chronicle based in my home city and county. The pack was sent to explore the disappearance of a suspected kinfolk lupus. When the characters arrived at the zoo they found in addition to the missing wolf, a coyote, and a mountain lion. The mountain lion was actually a Pumonica newly changed. This fit into my story otherwise I would have used a &quot;lost cub&quot; theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T03:52:39-08:00","id":769087,"title":"","content":"Hi!<br /> <br /> While I play and ST mostly VtM among the WoD systems, I have enough experience with WtA as well to state that the average numbers in the books are suboptimal, be it VtM or WtA. There are regions on Earth where the supernaturals are much more numerous than average and regions where they are even more rare.<br /> e.g If the set-up structure and &quot;food economy&quot; is well-made, you can play a fun VtM game in a few villages. The same goes for WtA. Caerns and Kinfolk are the operating variables. Esp. just lower-rank Caerns make for a more &quot;familiar&quot; game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7492-g\u00fcnther","name":"G\u00fcnther","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T05:59:57-08:00","id":769165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/765215-how-common-should-changing-breeds-be#post765215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But now I realise that, well, my game might as well be a <b>trip to the zoo</b>. Yeah, they're not going to be introduced all at once, and I can put a story or two around each of them (especially the Rokea, but the rhino really is there primarily for a bizarre surprise) Mix them in with fomori, ghouls, Leeches, spirits, that one cult, and maybe a mage if enough things go wrong, and you've essentially got a very colourful world of darkness. These things are supposed to be rare, but how rare?</div> </div> </div> </div>I had the same problem with the bloodlines in Vampire the Masquerade (bloodlines are rare families of vampires, dissimilar from the &quot;main&quot; clans). So in the &quot;good&quot; side (Camarilla) I usually put about 1 member of the bloodlines for each 7 normal vampires. On the &quot;evil&quot; side (Sabbat) they are more widespread, so 1:4 is still an acceptable rate. On the &quot;neutral&quot; side (Indipendents) the rate shift from 1:5 to 1:10 (depending from the city).<br /> <br /> I think these numbers can be applied to Werewolf too. Count how much Gaian Garou do you have in city, then you can add about 1 &quot;gaian&quot; shapeshifter from every 7 of them. Same with the Wyrm, 1 wyrmish shapeshifter for every 4 Black Spiral Dancers. As for the &quot;Indipendents&quot; (Weaver, or <u><b>pure</b></u> Wyld), use the Gaian Garou as measuring meter and add 1 non-aligned shifter for each 5 to 10 Gaians.<br /> Also, keep in mind that<br /> -Ratkin (usually, pure Wyld side) are supposedly roughly numerous as the Garou, but they aren't probably as well organized, so... while your chronicle could have a standard population of 30 Garou and 5-6 Ratkin, the Ratkin could, given enough time, call in their buddies for plot-necessity,<br /> -Ananasi: Spiders are widespread, the Ananasi too, maybe they too are numerous as the Garou. But they are separate around 3 warring camps (ananasa/weaver, pure wyld and pure wyrm), and is a little intricate, so you may prefer to not focus too much on them if you chronicle is Garou-based.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Keep in mind that these numbers are made simply for the sake of the setting, if your narrative necessities require otherwise, priority goes to the story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":515,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","user":"Ryoga84","date":". 11-19-2015, 09:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T06:41:22-08:00","id":769193,"title":"","content":"Ratkin have a big secret. They're way more numerous then the Garou. Oooops.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}